CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ true-constrained sole template is viable: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [temp.deduct]/8: the sole function template `f`'s non-deduced defaulted
template parameter substitutes to `enable_if<true,int>::type` == int (a valid
substitution), so `f` is viable and `f(5)` selects it.  Well-formed counterpart
of cpp11_sole_template_false_constraint; guards against over-rejecting a true
constraint when the sole candidate's defaulted parameter is checked.
